      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effects of electrocoagulation of caudomedial portion of the left and right cingulum bundles on tail-flick latency and vocalization threshold were examined on rats. We revealed a tendency to a decrease in the tail-flick latency and more pronounced elevation of the vocalization threshold after destruction of the right cingulum bundle. These findings indicate functional asymmetry of the cingulum bundle in the realization of the emotional nociceptive reaction."},
